	(text_box "USB\n\nSOC has:\n1 USB OTG\n- We will use this as 'peripheral' and source power from it\n3 USB hosts\n- 1 with usb PHY\n- 2 with HSIC\n\nCC pins:\n\nUSB_OTG_CHD_B: NC\nSenses charger detect and tells PMIC if batter should be charged.\nWe might do a standard ADC for CC voltage check only for logging, not for high power drain\n\nUSB_OTG_VBUS:\nPower input from UFP VBUS if powered from USB\nPower input from PMIC VIN if powered from 3.3 directly\nFeeds LDO_USB\nDo not connect to Host USB side\n\nUSB_H1_VBUS:\nAnother input into LDO_USB\n\nQuestion:\n- Should USB host be powered by USB OTG's VBUS, or should we gate it in some way (through PMIC?)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 424.18 7.62 0)
		(size 111.76 73.66)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "028d1a02-d15f-4a64-8dcc-dc2edc0c3ae2")
	)
	(text_box "Unused switching regulators should be connected as follow: Pins SWxLX and SWxFB should be unconnected and Pin SWxIN should be\nconnected to VIN with a 0.1 μF bypass capacitor.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 266.7 0)
		(size 48.26 17.78)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "67c2b2b4-f68e-4135-9981-45739dcbc151")
	)
	(text_box "INTERNAL LDOS\n\nVDD_HIGH_CAP  = 204mA\n - SATA_VPH = 13 + 7 = 20mA\n - PCIE_VPH = 20mA\n - HDMI_VPH = 14mA\n - MIPI     = ??\n - LVDS     = ??\n - GETH_2V5 = 150mA\nVDD_SOC_CAP  = 69.1mA\n - SATA_VP = 18mA\n - PCIE_VP = 47mA\n - HDMI_VP = 4.1mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 142.24 0)
		(size 40.64 27.94)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "81da9bec-2e9f-43cd-bf56-b398cb396ed6")
	)
	(text_box "PWR SEQ and assignment MMPF0100F0ANES (F0 OTP mode)\n\n1- VDD_SNVS_IN powered first (3.0V)\n\n2- POR_B asserted low until VDD_ARM_CAP VDD_SOC_CAP VDD_PU_CAP stable\n\n3- VDD_ARM_IN(996MHz max) and VDD_SOC_IN any order (1.375)\n\n==================================\n5V from USB OTG\nRT8070 outputs 3.3V from this and outputs to:\n- PMIC\n- AP2012 LCD backlight\n- HDMI connector\n\n==================================\nBoth modes:\nPMIC Inputs 3.3-4.2V and outputs:\n\nSEQ0: VSNVS\nVDD_SNVS_IN 3.0V (max 275uA)\n\nSEQ1:  SW1AB		1.375V		(max 2.5A)\nVDDARM_IN						(max 2.5A)\n\nSEQ2: SW1C		1.375V			(max 2.0A)\nVDDSOC_IN						(max 3.7A)  !!!\n\nSEQ3: SW3AB + VREFDDR	1.5V	(max 2.5A)\nNVCC_DRAM + NVCC_RGMII\n\nSEQ5: SW2 3.3V/3.0V					(max 2.0A)\nVDD_HIGH_IN (max 125mA + anything from HIGH_CAP)\nAlso 2.5V via LDO_2P5/VDD_HIGH_CAP:\nNVCC_LVDS2P5\nAlso 1.1V via LDO_1P1/NVCC_PLL_OUT\n======================================\nDEFAULT MODE\nSW4 = 1.8V unused SWBST = off\nVGEN3 = 0 (we program this 1.0V for ETH)\n\nF0 MODE\nSW4 = 3.15V unused SWBST = 5V\nVGEN3 = 2.5V !!! (do not enable F0 with this connected.\n======================================\n- To simplify, we'll not use SW4 SWBST or any VGENS\n- We'll use default mode to start out, jumper selectable\n- The main decision is to use USB power or bypass RT3070 and just get pin power\n- DDRVREF is available but we'll still use a resistor dividor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 309.88 104.14 0)
		(size 96.52 101.6)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8fff0652-401b-48aa-84f0-e6317810f3ab")
	)
	(text_box "UNPOWERED\n\n\nVREF_DDR\nAny VGEN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.16 254 0)
		(size 81.28 27.94)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "90bd74da-2359-44f3-a4a1-efda7356fd41")
	)
	(text_box "POWER REQUIREMENTS\n==================\nMax gaming power needed:\nVDD_ARM = 1625mA (2069 mW)\nVDD_SOC = 1250 (1555mW)\nVDD_HIGH = 54mA85 (126 mW)\nVDD_DDR +chip = 1390 (1995 mW)\nTotal = 6W max!\neMMC max = 100mA @ 3.3\nNAND max = 35mA @ 3.3 (116 mW)\nLCD logic = 3.3v 220mA\nVSC8531XMW-02\nSATA / PCIE ?\nWifi/RTL8723BS = 3.3v 150mA\n==================\n5V requirements outside of the PMIC:\nLCD backlight max = 45mA @ 18v + AP3012 waste (81% eff) = 1.6W max\nHDMI TPD12S016PWR = 100mA max (Keep on USB_SYS, not used on battery)\nUSB host port = ? (Keep on USB_SYS, not used on battery)\n==================\n8W absolute max.\nDhrystone is 3W + lcd + eMMC. We'll need this frequently\nNone of the PMIC DCDCs need more than 1.6A\n==================\nWe need:\n3.0 for snvs (ldo or common with vdd_high)\n1.15 to 1.4 DVS. Vdd_arm\n1.15 to 1.4 DVS. vdd_soc\n3.3 VDD_HIGH (can be comb with snvs). Maybe LCD bl of 1.2W too\n1.35 for ddr, else 1.5 for gige and ddr\n...\n3.3v for mem, \n2.5 eth, lvds. Hdmi pcie sata\n1.1 hdmi pcie sata\n1.0 for eth\n================================\nDESIGN\nAdd RT8070 (10W) to bring down USB power to 3.3-3.6V (VDDIO limit) of PF0100 VIN\n- Solder jumper picks between RT8070 or direct input of 3.3V(unsure of max)\nLCD BL AP3012 should connect directly to USB_SYS and enable pin to GPIO, defaulting to disable\nTwo 3.3Vs, DCDC 3.3 goes into VDD_HIGH_IN and another LDO powers outside peripherals after boot"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 309.88 12.7 0)
		(size 96.52 91.44)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a2c29460-5680-4e9d-afed-826fa67e1ada")
	)
	(text_box "BOOT MODE[1:0]\nb'00 = BT_FUSE_SEL ? Gpio boot (defaults SD) : serial download\nb'01 = Serial Downloader (USB OTG1 for 90 sec)\nb'10 = Internal boot\n\neMMC: SD3 8pin\n\nAlso can boot:\nSD1/uSDHC 4pin"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 12.7 0)
		(size 50.8 22.86)
